[ti:Ka Kau Question]
[ar:VESAHE · hkfaduio]
[al:Sanatan & Devotional]
[by:Radio Vaigyaaniq — draft timing, unverified]
[00:08.00]ekla chalo re... nahi...
[00:10.48]k.. ka... kaa... kaaa... kyaa...
[00:12.95]ka kau ke... ken kabhyaam kai...
[00:15.43]🎤 Narrator (Sanskrit / Nirukta 1.1):
[00:17.90]यास्कः कथयति –
[00:20.38]कः इति ब्रह्म। प्रश्नः एव सृष्टिः।
[00:25.33]🎵 Poet responds:
[00:27.80]kavim kaviim kavayah
[00:30.28]kahaam katham kathaam
[00:32.75]kasmin kyo keshu
[00:35.23]poet, to the poet, of poets
[00:37.70]where, how, what story
[00:40.18]in which? why? in the hairs…
[00:42.65]🎤 Narrator (Gurmukhi – Japji Sahib, Pauri 1):
[00:45.13]ੴ ਸਤਿ ਨਾਮੁ ਕਰਤਾ ਪੁਰਖੁ ਨਿਰਭਉ ਨਿਰਵੈਰੁ
[00:47.60]Ek aonkar sati namu karata purakhu nirabha-u niravairu
[00:52.55]🎵 Poet responds:
[00:55.03]ka kaa rahasya niraalaa
[00:57.50]kya kaun kab kaise kahan
[00:59.98]nai brahmaand racha daalaa
[01:02.45]the secret of 'ka' is strange
[01:04.93]what who when how where
[01:07.40]you just created a new universe
[01:09.88]🎤 Narrator (Devanagari – Kabir, Bijak, Ramaini 1):
[01:12.35]कंकर काहे करै तक़रीर
[01:14.83]काबा कौन, कौन बुतखाना
[01:17.30]Kankar kaahe karein taqeer
[01:19.78]Kaaba kaun, kaun but-khaana
[01:22.25](Why does a stone receive worship?
[01:24.73]What is Kaaba? What is a temple of idols?)
[01:27.20]🎵 Poet responds:
[01:29.68]khaali karo kya kahe kabeer
[01:32.15]kuttaa kaalaa kya jaane
[01:34.63]empty yourself, what does Kabir say
[01:37.10]what does a black dog know
[01:39.58]kaaba kaun, kaun but-khaana
[01:42.05]kaa de chakkar mein kaalaa phire
[01:44.53]what is Kaaba, what is the idol-house
[01:47.00]in the cycle of 'kaa', even the beloved wanders
[01:49.48]🎤 Narrator (Devanagari – Gorakhnath, Siddha Siddhanta Paddhati):
[01:51.95]नादात्मकं जगत्सर्वं
[01:54.43]नाद एव परं पदम्
[01:56.91]Nādatmakaṃ jagatsarvaṃ
[01:59.38]Nāda eva paraṃ padam
[02:01.86](The whole universe is made of sound.
[02:04.33]Sound alone is the supreme state.)
[02:06.81]🎵 Poet responds:
[02:09.28]khaak se kaaya, kaaya se kaam
[02:11.76]kaam se krodh, krodh se jaam
[02:14.23]dust to body, body to desire
[02:16.71]desire to anger, anger to death's wine
[02:19.18]kaun si kaayaa kaahe si kathaa
[02:21.66]kaa kaa rahasya – bas kaal kaa naath
[02:24.13]which body, what story
[02:26.61]the secret of 'ka' – just the Lord of Death/Time
[02:29.08]🎤 Narrator (Kannada – Allama Prabhu, Vachana 272):
[02:31.56]ಎಲ್ಲ ಕವಿಗಳು ಹೋದರು
[02:34.03]ಗುಹೇಶ್ವರನ ಲಿಂಗವ ಬಲ್ಲವರಾರು
[02:36.51]Ella kavigaḷu hōdaru
[02:38.98]Guhēśvarana liṅgava ballavarāru
[02:41.46](All poets have gone.
[02:43.93]Who knows Guheshwara’s Linga?)
[02:46.41]🎵 Poet responds:
[02:48.88]kahaam gaye sab kavim kaviim
[02:51.36]kavayah kaahe bane nayeem
[02:53.83]where have all poets gone
[02:56.31]why have the poets become so soft
[02:58.78]kasmin jag mein kyo nahi chain
[03:01.26]keshu hi to hai maaya mail
[03:03.73]in which world is there no rest
[03:06.21]it's in the hairs themselves – the filth of illusion
[03:08.68]🎤 Narrator (Gurmukhi – attributed: Chaupa Singh Rahitnama / Bachittar Natak bhava):
[03:11.16]ਕੜਾ, ਕਛੈਰਾ, ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ, ਕੰਘੀ, ਕੇਸ
[03:13.63]ਇਹ ਪੰਜ ਕਕਾਰੇ ਸਾਚੇ ਭੇਸ
[03:16.11]Kaṛā, kachaerā, kirpān, kanghī, kes
[03:18.58]Iha pañj kakāre sāce bhes
[03:21.06](Kada, kachera, kirpan, kangha, kesh –
[03:23.53]These five Ks are the true disguise.)
[03:26.01]🎵 Poet responds:
[03:28.48]e mera naanak we matwaalaa
[03:30.96]kaa de chakkar k nu dala
[03:33.43]oh my Nanak, you intoxicated one
[03:35.91]you threw me into the whirlpool of 'kaa
[03:38.38]kada kachcha karpaan kanghi kesh
[03:40.86]sakkhe purus nu ditte bhes
[03:43.33]bracelet, shorts, sword, comb, hair
[03:45.81]you gave disguise to the truest being
[03:48.29]chanddalaa de dna nai
[03:50.76]onnu wi dohkaa de daalaa
[03:53.24]not even a gift to the outcaste
[03:55.71]but you deceived even him
[03:58.19]🎤 Narrator (Panini / Sanskrit Grammarians, chanting):
[04:00.66]कः – कौ – के
[04:03.14]केन – काभ्याम् – कैः
[04:05.61]कस्मै – काभ्याम् – केभ्यः
[04:08.09]कस्मात् – काभ्याम् – केभ्यः
[04:10.56]कस्य – कयोः – केषाम्
[04:13.04]कस्मिन् – कयोः – केषु
[04:17.99]🎵 Poet responds:
[04:20.46]ka kau ke – teeno paal
[04:22.94]ken kabhyaam – dohe ka jaal
[04:25.41]ka, kau, ke – three worlds
[04:27.89]ken, kabhyaam – the net of duality
[04:30.36]kai – kaahe ko kai baar
[04:32.84]kathaam katham – kahta hai koi bichaar
[04:35.31]kai – why so many times
[04:37.79]kathaam katham – someone speaks a thought
[04:40.26]🎤 Narrator (Whispered, then loud):
[04:42.74]कः कः कः कः कः
[04:47.69]🎵 Poet (Solo):
[04:50.16]ka kaa rahasya – kya bataaye
[04:52.64]kya likhe kaghaz kya mitaaye
[04:55.11]the secret of 'ka' – how to tell
[04:57.59]what to write on paper, what to erase
[05:00.06]🎤 Narrator + Poet Together (Call and response style):
[05:02.54]Narrator asks Poet answers
[05:05.01]जेह? (jeh – which?) सो का (so ka – that 'ka')
[05:07.49]कवन? (kavan – what?) सो ख़ास (so khaas – that special one)
[05:09.96]कहाँ? (kahan – where?) सो ख़ंजर (so khanjar – that dagger)
[05:12.44]किस करण? (kis karan – for what reason?) सो किरण (so kiran – that ray)
[05:14.91]Final line – all together:
[05:17.39]so kaal – so khaas – so khanjar – so kiran
[05:19.86]that Time – that Special – that Dagger – that Ray
[05:22.34]k.. ka... kaa...
[05:24.81]kaaa...
[05:27.29]kyaa?
